{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAqrN56yjoCLiWsTkv3P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014vcowWJmN3bJ3wpMHcc8K2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-xpzBD5/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why `com.vk.nightly-review` has never reported anything\n\nTwo separate problems. The first hides the second, which is the real failure.\n\n## Cause 1 (fixed): `status` is a read-only variable in zsh\n\n`bin/nightly-review.zsh` line 19 was:\n\n```zsh\nstatus=$?\n```\n\nIn zsh, `status` is a built-in special parameter (an alias for `$?`) and cannot be assigned to. The assignment fails with:\n\n```\n/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n```\n\nThis is a fatal error in a non-interactive shell, so the script exits with status 1 right there. Everything after line 19 is skipped, including both the failure notice and the success notice. Nothing ever reaches Telegram, and no failure is reported.\n\nThis matches the captured state: `last exit code = 1`, and `nightly-review.err` contains the \"read-only variable: status\" line once per run. I reproduced it with zsh 5.9: the assignment aborts the script with exit 1 before the next line runs.\n\n**Fix:** renamed the variable to `rc` (`rc=$?`, and both uses in the `if` block). I tested the fixed script with a stub `claude` and a stub notifier in a scratch `HOME`:\n- when `claude` fails, it sends `nightly review FAILED (exit 1), see …` and exits 1;\n- when `claude` succeeds, it sends `nightly review done: …` and exits 0.\n\n## Cause 2 (not fixed here): `claude -p` is not logged in under launchd\n\n`nightly-review.err` shows, on every run:\n\n```\nNot logged in · Please run /login\n```\n\nSo the headless `claude -p` call fails, which is the real reason the job cannot produce a summary. The job itself runs (launchd finds `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` through the plist's PATH), but the agent has no credentials in that context.\n\nThis cannot be fixed from the snapshot, because it depends on your login state. Options:\n- Make sure the same user's login credentials are available to launchd's `gui/501` session. Running `claude` and `/login` interactively as `vk` is the usual first step, then re-run the job by hand with `launchctl kickstart gui/501/com.vk.nightly-review` to check.\n- Or provide an API key to the job by adding `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` under `EnvironmentVariables` in the plist. This stores a secret in a plist, so only do it if you're comfortable with that.\n\nOnce Cause 1 is fixed, you will get a `nightly review FAILED (exit 1)` Telegram message each night until Cause 2 is resolved. That is the intended behavior.\n\n## Things I could not verify\n\n- **Telegram token lookup under launchd.** `notify.sh` reads the token with `security find-generic-password -s tg-bot -w`. That works in a normal login session, but I can't check it in the launchd context from the snapshot. The notifier runs with `set -eu`, so if the lookup fails it exits silently. Check by running `launchctl kickstart` after fixing Cause 2, or by running the notifier under `env -i HOME=$HOME PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /bin/zsh -c '~/bin/notify.sh test'`.\n- **Whether `~/bin/nightly-review.zsh` on disk matches the snapshot.** I only changed the snapshot in this folder.\n\n## Applying the fix\n\nCopy the fixed script over the live one. The plist did not change, so no `launchctl` reload is needed; launchd reads the script fresh on each run:\n\n```sh\ncp bin/nightly-review.zsh ~/bin/nightly-review.zsh\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":989,"cache_read_input_tokens":29507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":989},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4054c89a-c420-4416-a0b5-7d689e31ffe2","uuid":"32ced375-dd04-44af-8eaa-70146a82c56b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:56:01.716Z","request_id":"req_011CgAqrMoEbSsZDUfoo7GXu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014vcowWJmN3bJ3wpMHcc8K2":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-xpzBD5/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why `com.vk.nightly-review` has never reported anything\n\nTwo separate problems. The first hides the second, which is the real failure.\n\n## Cause 1 (fixed): `status` is a read-only variable in zsh\n\n`bin/nightly-review.zsh` line 19 was:\n\n```zsh\nstatus=$?\n```\n\nIn zsh, `status` is a built-in special parameter (an alias for `$?`) and cannot be assigned to. The assignment fails with:\n\n```\n/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n```\n\nThis is a fatal error in a non-interactive shell, so the script exits with status 1 right there. Everything after line 19 is skipped, including both the failure notice and the success notice. Nothing ever reaches Telegram, and no failure is reported.\n\nThis matches the captured state: `last exit code = 1`, and `nightly-review.err` contains the \"read-only variable: status\" line once per run. I reproduced it with zsh 5.9: the assignment aborts the script with exit 1 before the next line runs.\n\n**Fix:** renamed the variable to `rc` (`rc=$?`, and both uses in the `if` block). I tested the fixed script with a stub `claude` and a stub notifier in a scratch `HOME`:\n- when `claude` fails, it sends `nightly review FAILED (exit 1), see …` and exits 1;\n- when `claude` succeeds, it sends `nightly review done: …` and exits 0.\n\n## Cause 2 (not fixed here): `claude -p` is not logged in under launchd\n\n`nightly-review.err` shows, on every run:\n\n```\nNot logged in · Please run /login\n```\n\nSo the headless `claude -p` call fails, which is the real reason the job cannot produce a summary. The job itself runs (launchd finds `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` through the plist's PATH), but the agent has no credentials in that context.\n\nThis cannot be fixed from the snapshot, because it depends on your login state. Options:\n- Make sure the same user's login credentials are available to launchd's `gui/501` session. Running `claude` and `/login` interactively as `vk` is the usual first step, then re-run the job by hand with `launchctl kickstart gui/501/com.vk.nightly-review` to check.\n- Or provide an API key to the job by adding `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` under `EnvironmentVariables` in the plist. This stores a secret in a plist, so only do it if you're comfortable with that.\n\nOnce Cause 1 is fixed, you will get a `nightly review FAILED (exit 1)` Telegram message each night until Cause 2 is resolved. That is the intended behavior.\n\n## Things I could not verify\n\n- **Telegram token lookup under launchd.** `notify.sh` reads the token with `security find-generic-password -s tg-bot -w`. That works in a normal login session, but I can't check it in the launchd context from the snapshot. The notifier runs with `set -eu`, so if the lookup fails it exits silently. Check by running `launchctl kickstart` after fixing Cause 2, or by running the notifier under `env -i HOME=$HOME PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /bin/zsh -c '~/bin/notify.sh test'`.\n- **Whether `~/bin/nightly-review.zsh` on disk matches the snapshot.** I only changed the snapshot in this folder.\n\n## Applying the fix\n\nCopy the fixed script over the live one. The plist did not change, so no `launchctl` reload is needed; launchd reads the script fresh on each run:\n\n```sh\ncp bin/nightly-review.zsh ~/bin/nightly-review.zsh\n```\n"}}}
