{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAqsBaMBvnJP97SvrcKp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has never reported anything for two reasons. The first is a bug that hid the second, and I fixed the bug.\n\n1. **Bug (fixed):** `bin/nightly-review.zsh` line 19 assigned `status=$?`. In zsh, `status` is read-only, so the script died there with exit 1 before reaching the Telegram notify calls. That is why nothing was sent, not even a failure notice. I renamed the variable to `rc`. A test with stub `claude` and notifier scripts confirmed that failures now send a \"FAILED (exit 1)\" message and successes send the summary.\n2. **Real failure (not fixed):** `nightly-review.err` shows `Not logged in · Please run /login` on every run, so the headless `claude -p` call never produces a review. This depends on your login state, which I can't see from the snapshot. ANSWER.md lists the options: log in as `vk` so launchd can use the credentials, or set an API key in the plist.\n\nOnce the fix is in place, you'll get a \"FAILED (exit 1)\" Telegram message each night until the login issue is resolved. The fix is only in this snapshot. To apply it, copy `bin/nightly-review.zsh` over `~/bin/nightly-review.zsh`. The plist is unchanged, so no reload is needed.\n\nI also couldn't verify that the Telegram token lookup (`security find-generic-password`) works under launchd. ANSWER.md explains how to check it.\n\nCauses, tests, and next steps are in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing was committed or sent anywhere external."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2213,"cache_read_input_tokens":30496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2213},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null}